<h1>Welcome to Quickfire Help</h1>
<p>Quickfire keeps this help pane right beside your work so you never lose your spot.</p>
<img src="/img/help/helpwelcome.png" style="height: 186px;" />
<h2>Find answers quickly</h2>
<p>Pick any topic on the left and it loads right away in this pane. Links open in a new tab so you can follow a guide and jump straight back.</p>
<p>Tap the refresh button in the help header if you update a page while Quickfire is open.</p>
<h2>What you can do</h2>
<p>Read Quickstart first to set your time zone, storage, and profile. Then browse Basics and Tips to learn shortcuts, automations, and voice commands.</p>
<p>Have your own team notes? Drop any .cshtml, .razor, or .html file into the help folder and it appears in the list. Keep the tone simple so everyone can follow along.</p>
<img src="/img/help/folder.jpg" style="height: 186px;" align="right" />
<h2>When you get stuck</h2>
<p>Use Troubleshooting for quick fixes, or contact the Quickfire team with the exact message you saw. We will handle the heavy lifting.</p>
